## Project overview

The UK flight delays ETL project is a self-directed project designed to practice building a complete ETL (Extract, Transform, Load) pipeline in pythn. 

The goal was to process raw flight data by:
* Extracting it from a csv file
* Cleaning and transforming it for consistency 
* Loading it into a PostgreSQL database for further analysis

This project has helped me strengthen my Python, SQL, and data engineering skills whilst also practacing unit testing with database mocking.

The project was built as part of my learning journey during the Data Engineering Bootcamp, but it was entierly designed and implemented by me. 
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Modules

Raw_data - Folder containing the CSV file with raw uk flight delay data used for extraction 

Flight_delays.py - Comtains the main ETL functions. Handles the full process of extracting flight delay data, cleaning and transforming it and loading it into a PostgreSQL datatbase

run_etl - Runs the entire ETL pipline by calling the functions from flight_deays.py. Prints helpful progress, successfull/failure messages to the terminal. 

test_flight_delays.py - Includes all unit testing for all three ETL stages. Testing happy and unhappy cases. 
